{"author": "person-f1c49678", "body": "## What happened

Flaky test detected: 

`[rfe_id:96338][crit:medium][vendor:[email removed]][level:component]Taints and toleration`

/kind flake

/sig compute

## Additional context

This test works by first selecting a node that is currently running Proj pods, tainting it with `CriticalAddonsOnly:NoExecute`, and asserting that those Proj pods remain running/not evicted (i.e. tolerate the taint). 

The failure is commonly hit in the test’s AfterEach cleanup: after removing the `CriticalAddonsOnly:NoExecute` taint, it waits (60s) for all deployments that had pods on the tainted node to have ReadyReplicas >= 1.

Kubemacpool appears not to tolerate `CriticalAddonsOnly:NoExecute` and can take longer than 60s to become Ready again, so the cleanup times out even if the actual Proj “taint/toleration” intent succeeded.

```
// AfterEach: wait for every deployment that had pods on the tainted node to recover
Eventually(func(g Gomega) {
  for _, nn := range deploymentsOnNode {
    deployment, err := virtClient.AppsV1().Deployments(nn.Namespace).Get(ctx, nn.Name, opts)
    // skip NotFound / deleting / scaled-to-zero
    g.Expect(deployment.Status.ReadyReplicas).To(BeNumerically(">=", 1), fmt.Sprintf("Deployment %s is not ready", nn))
  }
}, time.Minute, time.Second).Should(Succeed())
```

## Suggestion

Since this is primarily validating generic Kubernetes taint/toleration behavior, consider removing this test.", "closed_by": null, "comments": [], "created_at": "2026-02-19T23:45:55Z", "duplicate_of": null, "labels": ["kind/flake", "sig/compute"], "missing": [], "number": 57503, "references": [{"at": "2026-02-20T14:26:11Z", "kind": "cross_reference", "number": 16903, "type": "PullRequest", "will_close": false}], "state": "OPEN", "state_reason": null, "title": "[Flake] suggest removing [rfe_id:96338] taints-and-tolerations test (not Proj-specific; flakes on kubemacpool)", "url": "https://host-623.example/proj/proj/issues/57503"}
